ed by Sam Corlett. In the front office, owner Hal Durkin, played by William H. Macy, must decide which of his two daughters — played by Mandy Moore and Chloe Bennet — is equipped to eventually inherit the team. The ensemble also includes Chace Crawford, Tanner Zagarino, Bridget Moynahan and Omar Epps.","## A draft moment staged for the cameras","In a bit of showmanship that blurred fiction and reality, the series staged a fake draft announcement at the real 2026 NFL draft in Pittsburgh: commissioner Roger Goodell took the stage to announce the fictional Connor Roarke as Cleveland’s first pick. The moment was filmed for the series and was not an actual selection. Macy, who praised the scripts as “Shakespearean” in remarks to Deadline, noted the NFL’s full backing: the league is co-producing, so the production has complete access.","## When and where to watch","“The Land” premieres February 15 on Hulu in the United States — and on Hulu via Disney+ for bundle subscribers — with Disney+ carrying it internationally, including a February 15, 2027 launch in Australia. The show’s tagline sets the tone: “When the game is over, the real drama begins.”"],"sources":[{"name":"ESPN — Cleveland Browns gets their close-up in first trailer for Hulu’s ‘The Land’","role":"primary","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50177761/cleveland-browns-land-hulu-trailer"},{"name":"Hypebeast — Hulu ‘The Land’ trailer: Christopher Meloni, William H. Macy","role":"corroboration","url":"https://hypebeast.com/2026/10/christopher-meloni-william-h-macy-hulu-the-land-official-trailer-release-info"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"checkedAt":"2026-10-14T19:09:09Z","notes":"ESPN (read live 2026-10-14 via browser task) + Hypebeast + Consequence: Hulu debuted first trailer for “The Land,” scripted drama about fictional Cleveland Browns; creator Dan Fogelman; cast Christopher Meloni (coach Danny Roarke), William H. Macy (owner Hal Durkin), Sam Corlett (QB son Connor Roarke), Mandy Moore, Chace Crawford, Chloe Bennet, Bridget Moynahan, Omar Epps, Tanner Zagarino; NFL co-producing with authentic branding; Goodell’s staged draft announcement at 2026 Pittsburgh draft; premieres Feb 15 (day after Super Bowl LXI) on Hulu. No superseding development."}},{"id":"art-0113-anthropic-q3-revenue-2026","slug":"anthropic-q3-revenue-16-8-billion-ahead-of-ipo","headline":"Anthropic’s Quarterly Revenue Jumps to $16.8 Billion as IPO Preparations Accelerate","socialHeadline":"Anthropic hit $16.8B in Q3 revenue — up 45% — as it gears up for a blockbuster IPO","summary":"Anthropic’s revenue surged about 45% to $16.8 billion in the third quarter of 2026, figures shared at a pre-IPO investor day suggest, as the AI company targets a stock-market listing before year-end at a valuation above $1.8 trillion.","category":"Artificial Intelligence","tags":["Anthropic","IPO","artificial intelligence","revenue","Claude"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":true,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-anthropic-q3-revenue-0-c23f3931-95d9-48f9-8f6c-404045043ccc.webp","alt":"Illustration of an AI chip with a neural-network brain and rising revenue bars","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["Anthropic’s revenue accelerated sharply in the third quarter of 2026, climbing roughly 45 percent to $16.8 billion as the artificial-intelligence company courts investors ahead of a long-awaited stock-market listing, according to figures reported by Reuters and the Wall Street Journal on Wednesday.","The numbers were shared with attendees at a pre-IPO investor day held at Anthropic’s San Francisco headquarters on October 14, Reuters reported, citing an investor who was present. They show revenue rising from about $4.7 billion in the first quarter to $11.6 billion in the second, putting nine-month 2026 revenue at roughly $33 billion. Anthropic also told investors it was profitable on an adjusted basis in the third quarter. Anthropic itself declined to comment, and the figures were not published by the company directly — they come from attendees via two independent news organizations.","## The IPO timeline","The investor day is the clearest signal yet that Anthropic’s public listing is close. The Wall Street Journal reported that the company is targeting formal IPO marketing as early as the week of November 9, with a trading debut possible before Thanksgiving or by the end of the year, at a valuation of $1.8 trillion or more. The Journal also reported the offering could raise up to $100 billion. At that valuation, the listing would rank among the largest stock-market debuts in history.","## The spending behind the growth","The revenue surge comes alongside staggering commitments to the infrastructure that powers AI models. Anthropic has committed at least $518 billion over a decade to cloud, compute and infrastructure spending, a scale of outlay that explains both its growth and its hunger for fresh capital. For context, the company’s full-year 2025 revenue was about $4.6 billion — itself twelve times the prior year — while it posted an operating loss of more than $8 billion."],"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — Anthropic’s Q3 revenue surges 45% to nearly $17 billion","role":"primary","url":"https://www.wysl1040.com/anthropics-q3-revenue-surges-45-to-nearly-17-billion/"},{"name":"Wall Street Journal — Anthropic’s quarterly revenue jumped 45% to nearly $17 billion","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/anthropics-quarterly-revenue-jumped-45-to-nearly-17-billion-1c7e28b8"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Reuters (Oct 14, investor who attended the SF pre-IPO investor day) + WSJ (people familiar) independently confirmed Q3 2026 revenue $16.8bn (+45% from Q2 $11.6bn; Q1 ~$4.7bn), profitable on adjusted basis in Q3, IPO formal marketing as early as week of Nov 9, debut before Thanksgiving or by year-end, $1.8-2tn+ valuation, up to $100bn raise; 2025 full-year ~$4.6bn (12x 2024) with >$8bn operating loss; nine-month 2026 ~$33bn; $518bn decade compute commitment. Caveat recorded: figures from attendees via Reuters/WSJ, not an official Anthropic statement (company declined comment). No superseding statement as of 2026-10-15.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z"}},{"id":"art-0114-north-korea-submarine-missiles-2026","slug":"north-korea-tests-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles","headline":"North Korea Says It Test-Fired Submarine-Launched Cruise Missiles","socialHeadline":"North Korea says it tested two submarine-launched cruise missiles on Wednesday, state media reports","summary":"North Korean state media said the country test-fired two types of submarine-launched strategic cruise missiles on Wednesday in what Pyongyang described as a navy training exercise; South Korea’s military had not publicly confirmed the launches.","category":"World","tags":["North Korea","missiles","KCNA","East Sea","South Korea"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":true,"editorPick":true,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-north-korea-slcm-0-326d6331-d07c-4d88-b95c-b98ab49e7ea3.webp","alt":"Illustration of a submarine launching missiles beneath stylized waves","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["North Korea said on Wednesday that it had test-fired two types of submarine-launched strategic cruise missiles, describing the launches as part of a navy training exercise, state media reported.","The Korean Central News Agency (KCNA) said the missiles were launched into the East Sea, also known as the Sea of Japan, and claimed there was no adverse impact on the security of neighboring countries. The agency said the tests were intended to check the operational readiness of underwater combat systems. Senior officials observed the exercise, including Kim Jong-sik, a first vice department director of the Workers’ Party Central Committee, and Jang Chang-ha, head of the Missile Administration. KCNA gave no further details on the launch location or the missiles’ flight performance, and the report appeared on KCNA’s wire only, not in the domestic Rodong Sinmun newspaper.","## No confirmation from Seoul","South Korea’s military authorities had not publicly announced or commented on the launches as of Thursday, a notable gap that leaves the test confirmed only through Pyongyang’s own account. Independent analysts note that North Korea’s modern missile submarine is not believed to be fully operational, so even the platform used for the test remains unclear from the state-media account alone.","## Rising tensions","The test follows weeks of friction on the peninsula. A landmine blast in the Demilitarized Zone on September 21 injured three South Korean soldiers, and North Korea has run multiple missile tests through October. NewsVeria will update this story if South Korea or the United States publicly confirms or disputes the launch."],"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — North Korea says it tested submarine-launched cruise missiles, KCNA says","role":"primary","url":"https://wnflsports.com/2026/10/14/north-korea-says-it-tested-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles-kcna-says/"},{"name":"Aju Press — KCNA reports Oct 14 SLCM tests; ROK military yet to comment","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.ajupress.com/view/20261015081402939"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Reuters (Seoul, Oct 15) + Aju Press (Seoul, Oct 15) report KCNA’s Oct 15 announcement verbatim: two types of submarine-launched strategic cruise missiles test-fired Oct 14 into the East Sea as a navy training exercise to verify underwater combat readiness; observers Kim Jong-sik (WPK first vice department director) and Jang Chang-ha (Missile Administration head); KCNA gave no launch-location or flight-performance details; report on KCNA only, not Rodong Sinmun; ROK military had not publicly announced/commented as of Oct 15; modern missile submarine not believed fully operational; context of Sept 21 DMZ landmine blast injuring three ROK soldiers and multiple October DPRK tests. Framed throughout as a reported state-media claim with the attribution caveat. No superseding confirmation as of 2026-10-15.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z"}},{"id":"art-0115-trump-greenland-oil-exploration-2026","slug":"trump-greenland-oil-gas-mineral-exploration-truth-social","headline":"Trump Claims “Massive” Greenland Oil and Mineral Exploration Is About to Begin; Nuuk Pushes Back","socialHeadline":"Trump says massive oil and mineral exploration is “getting ready to begin” in Greenland — Nuuk disagrees","summary":"President Donald Trump declared on Truth Social that “massive” oil, gas and mineral exploration is getting ready to begin in Greenland, but Greenland’s government pushed back, saying the island is “very far away from ‘massive’ exploration.”","category":"World","tags":["Greenland","Donald Trump","oil","minerals","Denmark"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-trump-greenland-oil-0-27e8a0c9-bb03-420c-a5b3-73d2142d53df.webp","alt":"Illustration of a stylized Greenland map with oil derricks and mineral crystals","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["President Donald Trump declared on Wednesday that “massive” oil, gas and mineral exploration is “getting ready to begin” in Greenland — a claim swiftly disputed by Greenland’s own government.","In a post on Truth Social early Wednesday, Trump wrote: “Massive Oil, Gas, and Mineral Exploration is getting ready to begin in our new and beautiful Greenland!” He claimed “experts” say the amount of easily available oil is far greater than that of almost any land anywhere in the world. The post came a day after a campaign appearance in Alaska and followed last month’s US-Denmark-Greenland security agreement, which provided for two new military bases and the Golden Dome missile-defense system.","## Nuuk pushes back","Greenland’s government rejected the announcement’s immediacy. Deputy mining minister Jørgen Hammeken-Holm said “we are very far away from ‘massive’ exploration,” noting that smaller exploration efforts could take years to become operational. Denmark’s Foreign Ministry said resource access must follow Greenlandic legislation and that the security agreement granted US investors no preferential rights. Trump’s post named no specific deals, timelines or projects. Greenland has maintained a moratorium on new oil-exploration permits since 2021.","## What actually exists","The only concrete drilling plan on the horizon belongs to a Texas firm, Greenland Energy, which aims to drill in 2027 at an untested basin on the island’s east coast — but the company does not yet hold its own permit. Markets, however, moved fast: shares of 80 Mile PLC, an AIM-listed company that describes itself as custodian of Greenland’s three largest commodity projects, rose about 23 percent on the news."],"sources":[{"name":"CNN — Trump says massive oil, gas and mineral exploration set to begin in Greenland","role":"primary","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/14/politics/trump-greenland-oil-gas-minerals-intl-hnk?cid=external-feeds_iluminar_meta"},{"name":"The Hill — Trump: massive oil, gas, mineral exploration set to begin in Greenland","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.wcia.com/news/national/trump-massive-oil-gas-mineral-exploration-set-to-begin-in-greenland/"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"CNN (Oct 14) quotes Trump’s Truth Social post verbatim (“Massive Oil, Gas, and Mineral Exploration is getting ready to begin in our new and beautiful Greenland!”) + The Hill independently: post early Wednesday Oct 14 after Tuesday Alaska appearance; followed last month’s US-Denmark-Greenland security agreement (two new bases, Golden Dome); Greenland deputy mining minister Jørgen Hammeken-Holm pushback (“very far away from ‘massive’ exploration”); Denmark Foreign Ministry: access under Greenlandic law, no preferential US rights; no deals/timelines/projects named; 2021 moratorium on new oil permits stands; Greenland Energy 2027 east-coast plan without own permit; 80 Mile PLC +~23%. Necessary counterpoint included. No superseding development as of 2026-10-15.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z"}},{"id":"art-0116-psg-man-city-champions-league-2026","slug":"psg-beat-man-city-4-2-champions-league-haaland-brace-etihad","headline":"PSG End Manchester City’s Winning Run With 4-2 Champions League Thriller at the Etihad","socialHeadline":"PSG 4-2 Man City: the defending champions go 3-0 up at half-time and survive a Haaland-inspired fightback","summary":"Paris Saint-Germain raced into a 3-0 half-time lead and held off a Manchester City fightback to win 4-2 at the Etihad, ending the hosts’ eight-match winning run in the Champions League.","category":"Sports","tags":["PSG","Manchester City","Champions League","Erling Haaland","football"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":true,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-psg-man-city-4-2-0-fd8469e9-4015-42d4-a8b1-5ee6a317d4a5.webp","alt":"Illustration of a football stadium with pennants and goal nets showing a 4-2 scoreline","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["Paris Saint-Germain, the defending European champions, ended Manchester City’s eight-match winning run with a thrilling 4-2 Champions League victory at the Etihad Stadium on Wednesday night.","PSG blew City away in the first half of the league-phase Matchday 2 tie: Désiré Doué struck in the 13th minute, Ousmane Dembélé doubled the lead two minutes later, and Vitinha made it 3-0 in the 32nd. City roared back after the break through two Erling Haaland goals in the 53rd and 75th minutes, but Maghnes Akliouche’s 62nd-minute strike — PSG’s fourth — proved decisive, and Gianluigi Donnarumma saved a late Ferran Torres penalty to preserve the two-goal margin.","## Haaland’s record night in defeat","Haaland’s brace made him Manchester City’s all-time leading scorer in the Champions League, a personal milestone on a night his team came up short. It was a reminder of his extraordinary scoring rate in Europe — even in a losing cause against the continent’s finest defense.","## Group picture","The result leaves PSG top of their group with six points from two games and firmly in control of their title defense. For City, managed by Enzo Maresca with Pep Guardiola watching from the Etihad stands, it was a first defeat after eight straight wins — and a measure of the gap they must close to reclaim the European crown."],"sources":[{"name":"Sky Sports — Manchester City vs Paris Saint-Germain live (match data)","role":"primary","url":"https://www.skysports.com/football/manchester-city-vs-paris-saint-germain/live/577628"},{"name":"The Times — Champions League latest: Liverpool, Manchester City, PSG","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.thetimes.com/sport/football/article/champions-league-latest-news-live-score-liverpool-manchester-city-psg-gxlx9hqx3"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Sky Sports match data + The Times live coverage + Reuters/Sportradar + ESPN: PSG 4-2 Man City, Etihad, Wed Oct 14 2026, UCL 2026/27 league phase Matchday 2; half-time 3-0 (Doué 13’, Dembélé 15’, Vitinha 32’); Haaland 53’/75’ for City; Akliouche 62’ PSG fourth; Haaland brace = City’s all-time leading UCL scorer; ended City’s eight-match winning run; PSG top of group with 6 pts from 2; Guardiola in stands; Maresca manages City, Luis Enrique PSG; late Ferran Torres penalty saved by Donnarumma. Scoreline, scorers, date, venue consistent across sources. No superseding development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z"}},{"id":"art-0117-earhart-nikumaroro-expedition-2026","slug":"amelia-earhart-nikumaroro-expedition-taraia-object-2026","headline":"Expedition Begins Underwater Search for Amelia Earhart’s Plane at Nikumaroro","socialHeadline":"A 17-person expedition is scanning a Pacific lagoon for Amelia Earhart’s lost plane — answers could come in days","summary":"A joint Archaeological Legacy Institute–Purdue University expedition has begun an underwater survey off Nikumaroro in Kiribati, targeting a lagoon anomaly researchers believe could be Amelia Earhart’s Lockheed Electra, missing since 1937.","category":"Science","tags":["Amelia Earhart","Nikumaroro","archaeology","Purdue","aviation"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-earhart-nikumaroro-0-400d2525-fa78-42c4-a62c-de3b48e0c492.webp","alt":"Illustration of a vintage airplane silhouette and a magnifying glass over a Pacific island","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["A 17-person expedition has begun an underwater survey off a remote Pacific island in a bid to solve one of history’s most enduring mysteries: what happened to Amelia Earhart.","The Taraia Object expedition — a joint effort by the Archaeological Legacy Institute and Purdue University — arrived at Nikumaroro in Kiribati on Monday after a five-day, 830-nautical-mile voyage from Tarawa. Its target is the “Taraia Object,” a submerged anomaly in the island’s lagoon first spotted in 2020 satellite imagery and reportedly visible in aerial photographs since 1938, which researchers hypothesize could be Earhart’s Lockheed Electra 10-E.","## The search","The underwater survey began on October 14: a magnetometer will hunt for ferrous metals such as steel cabling, side-scan sonar will map buried objects, and a hydroprobe and water-induction dredge will follow up with visual inspection. The team expects to spend about five days on the island, and the anomaly remains unconfirmed — researchers plan to compare the rivet spacing and geometry of any aluminum skin they find against the Electra’s specifications, while critics have suggested the object may simply be a fallen tree. “It is incredibly rewarding to be this close to completing our inspection of the Taraia Object and potentially solving, at long last, the outstanding mystery of the disappearance of Amelia Earhart and Fred Noonan more than 89 years ago,” said Rick Pettigrew, the institute’s executive director.","## Why Purdue","Purdue’s involvement is more than academic: the Purdue Research Foundation funded Earhart’s “Flying Laboratory” Electra through the Amelia Earhart Fund for Aeronautical Research, tying the university directly to the 1937 flight. Earhart and her navigator Fred Noonan disappeared on July 2, 1937, over the central Pacific near Howland Island. The current effort is the 20th organized search for the aircraft — but the first to put divers and instruments on this particular anomaly."],"sources":[{"name":"Purdue University — Earhart expedition update: crew arrives at Nikumaroro","role":"primary","url":"https://www.purdue.edu/newsroom/2026/Q4/earhart-expedition-update-crew-arrives-at-nikumaroro-launches-critical-phase-of-amelia-earhart-plane-search"},{"name":"USA Today — New search for Amelia Earhart’s plane","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.usatoday.com/story/graphics/2026/10/13/new-search-for-amelia-earhart-plane/91942170007/"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Purdue official press release (Oct 2026) + USA Today independently: 17-person Taraia Object expedition (Archaeological Legacy Institute + Purdue) arrived Nikumaroro, Kiribati, Mon Oct 12 after 5-day, 830-nautical-mile voyage from Tarawa; target submerged lagoon anomaly spotted in 2020 satellite imagery, visible in aerial photos since 1938, hypothesized to be Earhart’s Lockheed Electra 10-E; underwater survey began Oct 14 (magnetometer, side-scan sonar, hydroprobe, water induction dredge); ~5-day field phase; 20th organized search; Earhart + Fred Noonan disappeared July 2, 1937 near Howland Island; Purdue Research Foundation funded the Electra; Rick Pettigrew quote confirmed; anomaly unconfirmed (rivet-spacing comparison planned; critics suggest fallen tree). “Solved in days” framing is grounded in the field-phase timeline, not pure speculation. No superseding development as of 2026-10-15.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z"}},{"id":"art-0118-dr-congo-ebola-2026","slug":"dr-congo-ebola-cases-surpass-9000-deaths-4381-2026","headline":"DR Congo Ebola Outbreak Passes 9,000 Cases, Becoming the Country’s Deadliest","socialHeadline":"DR Congo’s Ebola outbreak has passed 9,000 confirmed cases and 4,381 deaths — its largest ever","summary":"The Democratic Republic of Congo’s Ebola outbreak has reached 9,066 confirmed cases and 4,381 deaths, health ministry figures show — the largest and deadliest Ebola outbreak in the country’s history.","category":"Health","tags":["Ebola","DR Congo","WHO","public health","Bundibugyo"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":true,"editorPick":true,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-dr-congo-ebola-0-d0188135-4e2c-4409-b20d-729b80abecef.webp","alt":"Illustration of an Africa outline with medical-cross, flask and shield symbols","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["The Democratic Republic of Congo’s Ebola outbreak has passed 9,000 confirmed cases, health ministry figures released on Tuesday show, making it the largest and deadliest Ebola outbreak in the country’s history.","The ministry reported 9,066 confirmed cases and 4,381 deaths, including 88 new confirmed cases in the latest update. The ministry warned that “community transmission remains a concern,” with a large share of deaths occurring outside treatment centers. ReliefWeb’s situation report #14, published the same day, independently confirmed the figures as of October 11.","## Scale of the outbreak","The outbreak has reached 65 health zones across seven provinces — Ituri, Bas-Uele, Haut-Uele, North Kivu, South Kivu, South Ubangi and Tshopo — with transmission centered in Ituri, indicating uncontrolled spread. It is caused by the rare Bundibugyo strain of the virus, for which there is no approved vaccine or specific treatment; the crude case-fatality rate stands at about 48.3 percent. Declared on May 15, 2026, the outbreak has eclipsed the 2018–2020 North Kivu epidemic (3,470 cases, 2,287 deaths) and is the second-largest Ebola outbreak ever recorded globally, after the 2014–2016 West Africa epidemic.","## Containment faltering","Containment efforts are faltering amid conflict with rebel groups, population movement, community mistrust and medical-supply shortages. The virus has already crossed borders: an imported case was confirmed in Kenya on October 5, in a patient who traveled from the DRC through Uganda to Nairobi and died; Uganda’s own outbreak has been declared over. The World Health Organization assesses the risk to land-border neighbors as high. Figures in this story come from the DRC health ministry and ReliefWeb situation reports; NewsVeria will update them as official counts are revised."],"sources":[{"name":"AP, via Ghana Mma — Congo’s confirmed Ebola cases exceed 9,000 as containment efforts falter","role":"primary","url":"https://www.ghanamma.com/2026/10/13/congos-confirmed-ebola-cases-exceed-9000-as-containment-efforts-falter/"},{"name":"ReliefWeb — Ebola outbreak DRC and region, situation report #14 (Oct 13, 2026)","role":"corroboration","url":"https://reliefweb.int/report/democratic-republic-congo/ebola-outbreak-drc-and-region-situation-report-14-october-13-2026"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"AP wire (Bunia, Congo, Oct 13) attributes 9,066 confirmed cases / 4,381 deaths to DRC health ministry data released Tue Oct 13 (incl. 88 new cases; “community transmission remains a concern”; large share of deaths outside treatment centers; 65 health zones across Ituri, Bas-Uele, Haut-Uele, North Kivu, South Kivu, South Ubangi, Tshopo; centered in Ituri) + ReliefWeb situation report #14 (Oct 13, 2026) independently confirms as of Oct 11 the same 9,066/4,381 figures; rare Bundibugyo strain, no approved vaccine/treatment, ~48.3% CFR; declared May 15, 2026, eclipsing 2018-2020 North Kivu epidemic (3,470/2,287); largest in DRC history, second-largest globally after 2014-2016 West Africa; Kenya imported case Oct 5 (DRC→Uganda→Nairobi, died); Uganda outbreak declared over; containment faltering amid conflict/movement/mistrust/shortages; WHO risk to land-border neighbors high. Meets the official-confirmation bar for high-impact public-health figures; all tolls attributed to ministry/ReliefWeb and flagged as subject to revision.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T01:40:25Z"}},{"id":"art-0119-leap-second-vote-2027","slug":"leap-second-vote-versailles-bipm-continuous-utc-2027","headline":"World Timekeepers Vote This Week on Scrapping the Leap Second for Good","socialHeadline":"69 nations are voting in Versailles on ending the leap second — continuous UTC could start in 2027","summary":"Delegates from 69 countries are voting this week at the 28th General Conference on Weights and Measures in Versailles on a resolution to scrap the leap second, moving to continuous UTC from May 2027.","category":"Science","tags":["leap second","UTC","BIPM","timekeeping","metrology"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":true,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-leap-second-utc-0-7db921e5-92bd-4277-a09f-98c9b4b9682f.webp","alt":"Illustration of a clock face with satellite and moon motifs","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["The world’s timekeepers are voting this week on whether to abolish the leap second — the occasional extra tick added to keep atomic clocks in step with the Earth’s rotation.","Delegates from 69 member states at the 28th General Conference on Weights and Measures (CGPM), meeting in Versailles from October 13 to 15, are considering Draft Resolution C. If adopted, it would move the world to continuous Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) effective May 20, 2027, allowing the gap between atomic time and solar time to grow to as much as 3,600 seconds — effectively replacing leap seconds with a rare “leap hour.”","## Why it matters","Leap seconds, inserted irregularly since 1972, are a headache for digital infrastructure: computer networks, financial systems and navigation satellites all assume time flows smoothly, and the surprise extra second has caused outages in the past. Tech companies have lobbied for years to end the practice.","## What else is on the table","The Versailles meeting is also weighing a redefinition of the second itself — tying it to optical atomic clocks rather than the caesium standard — and a dedicated lunar time standard for Moon missions. The vote outcome had not been confirmed at publication; NewsVeria will update this story when the CGPM announces its decision."],"sources":[{"name":"BIPM — CIPM 2026 Session I decisions (Draft Resolution C, 28th CGPM)","role":"primary","url":"https://www.bipm.org/documents/d/guest/cipm2026-session-i-decisions-en?download=true"},{"name":"CNN — Scientists vote on eliminating the leap second","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/13/science/leap-second-elimination-time-standard?cid=external-feeds_iluminar_meta"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"BIPM documents confirm 28th CGPM (69 member states, Versailles, Oct 13–15) voting on Draft Resolution C: continuous UTC effective 20 May 2027, |UT1−UTC| tolerance to 3,600s (“leap hour”); second-redefinition and lunar time standard also on the agenda. CNN independently corroborates the vote and its stakes. Vote outcome not confirmed at check time — article explicitly framed as vote underway this week; chronology checked.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z"}},{"id":"art-0120-brewers-dodgers-nlcs-2026","slug":"brewers-dodgers-nlcs-game-3-bauers-3-0-series-lead","headline":"Brewers One Win From World Series After Bauers’ Blast Seals 3–0 NLCS Lead Over Dodgers","socialHeadline":"Brewers stun Dodgers 6–2 in Game 3 — Jake Bauers’ 412-ft homer puts Milwaukee one win from the World Series","summary":"The Milwaukee Brewers beat the Los Angeles Dodgers 6–2 in Game 3 of the NLCS on Wednesday, taking a 3–0 series lead behind back-to-back seventh-inning home runs from Jake Bauers and Garrett Mitchell.","category":"Sports","tags":["MLB","NLCS","Milwaukee Brewers","Los Angeles Dodgers","Jake Bauers"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":true,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-brewers-dodgers-nlcs-0-743cfbf0-daf7-4773-8471-0fbc12f00134.webp","alt":"Illustration of a baseball diamond with a home-run trajectory arc","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["The Milwaukee Brewers are one victory away from the World Series after stunning the Los Angeles Dodgers 6–2 in Game 3 of the National League Championship Series at Dodger Stadium on Wednesday.","The game turned in the seventh inning, when Jake Bauers launched a go-ahead 412-foot home run on the 11th pitch of his at-bat. Garrett Mitchell followed immediately with a 428-foot solo shot off Blake Snell, breaking the game open and silencing the home crowd.","## Dodgers on the brink","No team in baseball history has ever come back from a 3–0 deficit in a best-of-seven series, leaving the Dodgers — chasing a third straight championship — facing elimination in Game 4 on Thursday.","## One more to go","Milwaukee’s pitching held the Dodgers’ powerful lineup in check all night. A win on Thursday would send the Brewers to the World Series and end the Dodgers’ bid for a three-peat."],"sources":[{"name":"ESPN — Brewers put Dodgers on ropes, seize 3-0 NLCS lead in Game 3","role":"primary","url":"https://www.espn.com/mlb/story/_/id/50186797/brewers-put-dodgers-ropes-seize-3-0-nlcs-lead-game-3"},{"name":"AP via TMJ4 — Brewers stun Dodgers with back-to-back homers in 7th, take 3-0 NLCS lead with 6-2 win","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.tmj4.com/sports/brewers-stun-dodgers-with-back-to-back-homers-in-7th-inning-and-take-3-0-lead-in-nlcs-with-6-2-win"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"ESPN game report confirms Brewers 6–2 win in NLCS Game 3 at Dodger Stadium on Oct 14, 2026: Bauers go-ahead 412-ft HR on 11th pitch of the 7th, Mitchell 428-ft solo off Snell; Brewers lead series 3–0; Game 4 Thursday. AP/TMJ4 independently corroborates score, inning, and HR details. Chronology checked; distinct game from art-0042 (Game 1).","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z"}},{"id":"art-0121-yamal-messi-record-2026","slug":"lamine-yamal-teenage-record-better-than-messi-barcelona","headline":"At 19, Lamine Yamal Is Outpacing Even Messi’s Teenage Numbers at Barcelona","socialHeadline":"Lamine Yamal has 17 goal contributions in 10 games — better than Messi managed as a teenager","summary":"Lamine Yamal’s blistering start to the 2026/27 season has him outperforming Lionel Messi’s teenage output at Barcelona, with 8 goals and 9 assists in 10 appearances — days before the Ballon d’Or vote.","category":"Sports","tags":["Lamine Yamal","Lionel Messi","Barcelona","Champions League","Ballon d’Or"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":true,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-yamal-messi-record-0-fceee8e3-356b-40a7-9ab3-cba048efbd0e.webp","alt":"Illustration of rising bar charts, a boot striking a ball and trophy stars","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["Lamine Yamal is doing something no teenager at Barcelona has done before — not even Lionel Messi. The 19-year-old has 8 goals and 9 assists in just 10 appearances this season, a 17-contribution haul that edges past Messi’s 14 goal involvements from his own teenage breakthrough campaign in 2008/09.","The latest statement came on Tuesday, when Yamal set up two goals within three minutes of each other in Barcelona’s 4–1 Champions League win at Galatasaray — a performance that underlined why he is the frontrunner for this season’s Ballon d’Or, with the vote roughly eleven days away.","## The Messi comparison","Comparisons with Messi have followed Yamal since his debut, but the numbers now give them real weight: at the same age, the Argentine had yet to match this rate of end product across a season’s opening stretch.","## What comes next","If Yamal sustains anything close to this pace, the Ballon d’Or race may be decided early — and Barcelona will feel increasingly confident that their generational talent is not just the next big thing, but the present one."],"sources":[{"name":"Al Jazeera — Is Lamine Yamal’s Barcelona record better than Messi’s as a teenager?","role":"primary","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/10/15/is-lamine-yamals-barcelona-record-better-than-messis-as-a-teenager"},{"name":"mercatoeleven — Lamine Yamal player statistics","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.mercatoeleven.com/players/37656179"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Al Jazeera (Oct 15, 2026) confirms: Yamal 8G+9A in 10 apps in 2026/27 vs Messi 14 contributions in 2008/09; 2 assists in 3 minutes in Barça’s 4–1 UCL win at Galatasaray (Oct 13); Ballon d’Or ~11 days out. Stats cross-checked via mercatoeleven. Framed as statistical comparison, not a claim of overall superiority; chronology checked.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z"}},{"id":"art-0122-uk-gdp-august-2026","slug":"uk-economy-grows-august-2026-gdp-01-healey-budget","headline":"UK Economy Unexpectedly Grows 0.1% in August Ahead of Chancellor’s First Budget","socialHeadline":"UK GDP grew 0.1% in August, beating forecasts of a 0.1% fall — “welcome news” says Chancellor Healey","summary":"The UK economy grew by 0.1% in August, official figures showed on Thursday, defying forecasts of a contraction and giving the Chancellor a boost ahead of his first Budget.","category":"Business","tags":["UK economy","GDP","ONS","Budget","Chancellor Healey"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":true,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-uk-gdp-august-0-7e498b60-5da4-439f-b55e-0ab4f7e98598.webp","alt":"Illustration of a rising chart over a London skyline with a clock tower","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["The UK economy grew by 0.1% in August, the Office for National Statistics said on Thursday, confounding economists who had expected a 0.1% contraction.","Growth was driven by production output, which rose 0.8%, while the dominant services sector was flat on the month. Chancellor Healey welcomed the figures as “welcome news” ahead of his first Budget.","## A boost before the Budget","The surprise expansion gives the Chancellor some breathing room as he prepares his first fiscal statement, with markets watching for how he balances growth ambitions against strained public finances.","## What economists say","Analysts cautioned that a single month’s data does not make a trend, with services — the engine of the UK economy — showing no growth. But after months of stagnation fears, any positive surprise will be seized on by a government desperate for momentum."],"sources":[{"name":"ONS — GDP monthly estimate, UK: August 2026","role":"primary","url":"https://www.ons.gov.uk/economy/grossdomesticproductgdp/bulletins/gdpmonthlyestimateuk/august2026"},{"name":"PA via Oldham Times — UK economy unexpectedly grows 0.1% in August","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.theoldhamtimes.co.uk/news/national/26638106.uk-economy-unexpectedly-grows-0-1-august/?ref=rss"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"ONS monthly GDP bulletin (released Oct 15, 2026) confirms +0.1% in August vs −0.1% forecast; production +0.8%, services flat; Chancellor Healey “welcome news” quote ahead of his first Budget. PA wire independently corroborates figures and quote. Event date = release date; chronology checked; no superseding data.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z"}},{"id":"art-0123-indonesia-dry-ice-2026","slug":"indonesia-dry-ice-trial-south-sumatra-haze-2026","headline":"Indonesia Tests Dropping Dry Ice From Planes to Blast Through Wildfire Haze","socialHeadline":"Indonesia is dropping 1.5 tonnes of dry ice over South Sumatra to clear choking wildfire haze","summary":"Indonesia began an experimental trial on Thursday, dropping 1.5 tonnes of dry ice from an aircraft over South Sumatra in a bid to disperse thick wildfire haze, on orders from President Prabowo.","category":"Science","tags":["Indonesia","haze","dry ice","South Sumatra","wildfires","Prabowo"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-indonesia-dry-ice-0-fdd7c030-4f25-4bb8-8b68-ab00494a2191.webp","alt":"Illustration of a plane releasing ice crystals over haze clouds above palm forest","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["Indonesia has begun an unusual experiment to clear the choking haze blanketing parts of Sumatra: dropping 1.5 tonnes of solid carbon dioxide — dry ice — from an aircraft over South Sumatra.","The trial, announced by the Coordinating Ministry on Wednesday and carried out on Thursday, aims to break up the layer of trapped haze particles and lift visibility from about 1 kilometre to 5 kilometres. The operation was ordered by President Prabowo Subianto as the annual wildfire haze again spreads across the region.","## How it is supposed to work","The extreme cold of the dry ice is intended to trigger condensation in the haze layer, encouraging particles to clump and fall — a technique related to cloud seeding, repurposed here against smoke rather than for rain.","## What happens next","Officials say Central Kalimantan will be next if the South Sumatra trial succeeds. The haze has already forced school closures in Timor-Leste and disrupted daily life across the region, adding urgency to finding new tools against the seasonal crisis."],"sources":[{"name":"CNA — Indonesia to test dry ice seeding to combat haze","role":"primary","url":"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/asia/indonesia-test-dry-ice-seeding-combat-haze-air-quality-visibility-6461586"},{"name":"worldrightnowlive (Guardian) — Indonesia fights fire with dry ice as toxic haze spreads across region","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.worldrightnowlive.com/story/indonesia-fights-fire-with-dry-ice-as-toxic-haze-spreads-across-region"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Coordinating Ministry announcement (Oct 14, via CNA) confirms first trial: 1.5t solid CO2 dropped by plane over South Sumatra on Oct 15 to disperse trapped haze (visibility goal 1→5km); ordered by President Prabowo; Central Kalimantan next if successful. Guardian-origin reporting corroborates trial details and regional haze context. Chronology checked; framed as trial, not proven result.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z"}},{"id":"art-0124-pope-leo-recovery-2026","slug":"pope-leo-xiv-recovery-breakfast-gemelli-oct-2026","headline":"Pope Leo XIV ‘Slept Well’ and Ate Breakfast as Vatican Reports Steady Recovery","socialHeadline":"Two days after lung surgery, the 71-year-old Pope slept well and had breakfast, the Vatican says","summary":"Pope Leo XIV spent a tranquil night in Rome’s Gemelli hospital and ate breakfast on Thursday, the Vatican said, two days after surgery to remove part of his right lung.","category":"World","tags":["Pope Leo XIV","Vatican","Gemelli hospital"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-pope-leo-recovery-0-a36d4bba-e9b5-46ae-9d69-9027e43938ab.webp","alt":"Illustration of St Peter’s dome silhouette with dawn sunburst and doves","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["Pope Leo XIV “slept well” overnight and ate breakfast on Thursday morning, the Vatican said, offering a reassuring update two days after the 71-year-old pontiff underwent lung surgery.","The Pope had a 90-minute operation at Rome’s Gemelli hospital on Tuesday to remove the lower lobe of his right lung, where doctors confirmed an adenocarcinoma — a form of lung cancer. Pathology results are still pending, and his public schedule has been cancelled until at least October 20.","## A careful recovery","The Vatican’s medical bulletins have described his post-operative course as steady. Thursday’s update — restful sleep and a normal breakfast — is the latest sign the pontiff is recovering as expected.","## What we know","All medical details in this story come from official Vatican statements as reported by the wire services. NewsVeria will update this developing story as the Holy See releases further bulletins; this report is a follow-up to our earlier coverage of the operation itself."],"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — Pope Leo had good night in hospital, Vatican says","role":"primary","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/pope-leo-had-good-night-hospital-vatican-says-2026-10-15/"},{"name":"AP via Reflector — Pope Leo spent a tranquil night in the hospital after cancer surgery, Vatican says","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.reflector.com/news/national/pope-leo-spent-a-tranquil-night-in-the-hospital-after-cancer-surgery-vatican-says/article_32074074-cf8c-5377-9cdb-79560357db5e.html"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Vatican statement of Oct 15 (via Reuters) confirms: 71-year-old Pope Leo XIV had a good night and ate breakfast, two days after Tuesday’s 90-minute Gemelli surgery removing lower lobe of right lung (adenocarcinoma confirmed); pathology pending; schedule cancelled until Oct 20. AP independently corroborates. Distinct follow-up to art-0030 (surgery coverage); all medical facts attributed to Vatican/wires; chronology checked.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T07:52:30Z"}},{"id":"art-0125-us-wholesale-inflation-september-2026","slug":"wholesale-inflation-jumps-most-in-four-years","headline":"US Wholesale Inflation Jumps by the Most in Four Years as Gasoline Prices Soar","socialHeadline":"Producer prices rose 1.3% in September — the sharpest monthly gain since March 2022 — as gasoline surged 20.3%, far above forecasts","summary":"US producer prices climbed 1.3% in September, the largest monthly increase since March 2022, as a 20.3% surge in gasoline prices pushed wholesale inflation far beyond economists' forecasts.","category":"Business","tags":["US economy","inflation","PPI","Bureau of Labor Statistics","Federal Reserve"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":true,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-wholesale-inflation-2026101-0-9dcf52b7-890c-4ff5-933f-fb5a2fc4abee.webp","alt":"Illustration of a rising bar chart with an upward arrow and an energy-flame motif on a navy background","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["US wholesale inflation accelerated sharply in September, with the producer price index for final demand rising 1.3% from August — the biggest monthly increase since March 2022 and well above the 0.5% gain economists had expected, according to data released Thursday by the Bureau of Labor Statistics.","The annual rate climbed to 6.3%, the highest since December 2022, against a 5.3% consensus forecast. Soaring fuel costs drove the surprise: gasoline prices leapt 20.3% in a single month, and final-demand energy prices jumped 10.8% — accounting for more than four-fifths of a 2.9% surge in goods prices, the largest monthly increase in that series since the BLS began tracking it in 2009.","## Underlying pressures broaden","Stripping out volatile food and energy costs, core producer prices rose 0.7% on the month, the fastest pace in five months, lifting the annual core rate to 5% — its highest since January 2023. A narrower gauge excluding food, energy and trade services climbed 0.5% on the month and 5% from a year earlier.","## What it means for rates","The hotter-than-expected reading lands at a delicate moment, with investors and policymakers scrutinizing every inflation signal for clues about the path of interest rates. Wholesale prices often feed through to consumer prices with a lag, making the September print a closely watched input for the months ahead."],"sources":[{"name":"US Bureau of Labor Statistics — Producer Price Index, September 2026 release","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ppi.nr0.htm","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — US producer prices post largest increase in 4-1/2 years","url":"https://www.reuters.com/business/us-producer-prices-post-largest-increase-4-12-years-september-2026-10-15/","role":"corroboration"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","notes":"BLS PPI September 2026 release (Oct 15, 2026): +1.3% m/m vs +0.5% expected (FactSet/Dow Jones); +6.3% y/y vs +5.3% expected; largest monthly gain since Mar 2022; gasoline +20.3%; final-demand energy +10.8% m/m; goods +2.9% m/m (largest since series began 2009); core +0.7% m/m (fastest in five months), 5% y/y (highest since Jan 2023). Figures identical across Reuters, CNN, Dow Jones Newswires and Barron's. Chronology checked; no superseding release."}},{"id":"art-0126-jon-rahm-liv-separation-2026","slug":"jon-rahm-reaches-separation-agreement-with-liv-golf-gives-up-nine-figure-contract","headline":"Jon Rahm Reaches Separation Deal With LIV Golf, Walking Away From Nine-Figure Contract","socialHeadline":"The deal ends all of Rahm's LIV contracts and returns his name, image and likeness rights — pending a judge's approval on Nov. 5","summary":"Jon Rahm and LIV Golf reached a separation agreement on Wednesday that terminates all his LIV contracts, forfeits his Legion XIII equity, and returns his name, image and likeness rights — pending bankruptcy-court approval on Nov. 5.","category":"Sports","tags":["Jon Rahm","LIV Golf","golf","Legion XIII"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-rahm-liv-separation-2026101-0-b8c7d45b-d516-4f7d-a454-94c78c6343dd.webp","alt":"Illustration of a torn golf contract with a flagstick and golf ball on a navy background","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["Jon Rahm has reached a separation agreement with LIV Golf that terminates all of his contracts with the breakaway tour, ending one of the most lucrative player deals in the sport's history, according to court records and reporting.","Under the agreement reached Wednesday, Rahm releases all monetary and economic claims against LIV, forfeits his equity in his Legion XIII team, and regains control of his name, image and likeness rights along with the Legion XIII intellectual property.","## Court approval still needed","The deal requires approval from Judge Michael B. Kaplan, who is scheduled to consider it on Nov. 5. Rahm is LIV's largest unsecured creditor, owed $7.5 million at the time of the tour's Chapter 11 filing on Sept. 8.","Rahm reportedly stood to collect more than $100 million over the remainder of a contract reported to be worth over $300 million when he signed in December 2023. A three-time LIV individual champion, he earned nearly $107 million on the course during his stint.","The separation follows a court hearing on Oct. 7 at which Rahm's lawyer, John Beck, told the court that the “LIV 2.0” terms offered to the Spaniard were “unacceptable.”"],"sources":[{"name":"U.S. Bankruptcy Court (D.N.J.) court records, via ESPN reporting","url":"https://players.bio/news/jon-rahm-reaches-separation-agreement-with/907626","role":"primary"},{"name":"Golfweek / USA Today — LIV Golf contract release report","url":"https://golfweek.usatoday.com/story/sports/golf/liv/2026/10/15/liv-golf-contract-release-bryson-dechambeau/92261338007/","role":"corroboration"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","notes":"Agreement reached Oct 14, 2026: all LIV contracts terminated; Legion XIII equity forfeited; NIL rights and team IP returned to Rahm; Judge Kaplan approval hearing Nov 5, 2026; Rahm largest unsecured creditor ($7.5M at Sept 8 Chapter 11 filing); reportedly $100M+ owed on $300M+ deal signed Dec 2023; 3x LIV individual champion; ~$107M on-course earnings; lawyer John Beck called 'LIV 2.0' terms 'unacceptable' on Oct 7. Corroborated by Golfweek/USA Today."}},{"id":"art-0127-starshield-ukraine-speed-limits-2026","slug":"what-is-starshield-who-limited-ukraines-access","headline":"Starshield Speed Limits Disrupted Ukraine's Drone Operations Before Access Was Restored","socialHeadline":"SpaceX imposed speed restrictions on its military satellite service without warning, Ukrainian officials said; connectivity was restored the next day","summary":"Overnight on October 13–14, speed restrictions were imposed on Starshield, the military-grade satellite internet service used by Ukraine, cutting connectivity on terminals moving faster than about 160 km/h and disrupting drone missions before access was restored.","category":"World","tags":["Ukraine","Starshield","SpaceX","Elon Musk","drones"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-starshield-ukraine-20261015-0-668f2f60-b991-4853-8f75-47c1e2c8642a.webp","alt":"Illustration of satellites beaming signals to a world map grid, with one signal path dimmed","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["Ukrainian drone operations were disrupted overnight on Oct. 13–14 after speed restrictions were imposed on Starshield, the military-grade satellite internet service operated by SpaceX, Ukrainian officials said — before access was restored the following day.","Serhiy Beskrestnov, a Ukrainian presidential adviser on defence technology, said via Telegram that the restrictions — set at about 100 miles per hour (160 km/h) on Starshield's “military package” — arrived with no prior warning to Ukrainian forces and disrupted multiple missions.","Elon Musk responded on Oct. 14, stating that “Starshield systems are owned and controlled by the US government” and that “any limits on speed or usage are decided by the US military and ultimately POTUS.”","## Access restored","Ukraine's defence minister, Mykhailo Fedorov, announced on Oct. 14 that connectivity at speeds up to 160 km/h was being restored, calling the removal of the limit entirely “critical for Ukraine's defense.”","President Volodymyr Zelensky, speaking on Piers Morgan Uncensored, called the throttling “a big mistake,” warning: “People will die.” Starshield is SpaceX's government and national-security satellite service, separate from the commercial Starlink network."],"sources":[{"name":"New York Post (Oct 14, 2026) — carries Musk's and Zelensky's direct statements","url":"https://nypost.com/2026/10/14/world-news/elon-musk-blames-trump-for-starshield-throttling-in-ukraine-that-zelenksy-warns-will-cost-lives/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Men's Journal via The New York Times (Oct 14, 2026) — Starshield explainer and throttling report","url":"https://www.mensjournal.com/news/what-is-starshield-inside-spacexs-military-grade-starlink-system-used-by-ukraine","role":"corroboration"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","notes":"Beskrestnov (Telegram, Oct 14): speed cap ~100 mph/160 km/h on 'military package', no warning, missions disrupted. Musk (Oct 14): Starshield owned/controlled by US government; limits decided by US military and POTUS. Fedorov (Oct 14): 160 km/h connectivity being restored; full removal 'critical'. Zelensky (Piers Morgan Uncensored, Oct 14): 'It's a big mistake. People will die.' Newer development incorporated: access restored Oct 14. All claims strictly attributed to the named speakers."}},{"id":"art-0128-nandy-sky-itv-takeover-2026","slug":"nandy-minded-to-intervene-sky-itv-takeover","headline":"Lisa Nandy “Minded to Intervene” in Sky's £1.6bn ITV Takeover","socialHeadline":"The Culture Secretary cited news plurality concerns and proposed a new public-interest test; Sky and ITV have until Oct. 20 to respond","summary":"Culture Secretary Lisa Nandy has told Parliament she is 'minded to' intervene in Sky's up-to-£1.6bn acquisition of ITV's media and entertainment arm, citing concerns over news plurality and proposing a new public-interest test for on-demand programming.","category":"Business","tags":["Sky","ITV","Lisa Nandy","UK media","takeovers"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-sky-itv-takeover-20261015-0-ebb3c2b4-0c0f-4ed0-a1d3-27f9fae4b4db.webp","alt":"Illustration of broadcast towers merging under a regulatory-review emblem on a navy background","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["Culture Secretary Lisa Nandy has told Parliament she is “minded to” intervene in Sky's proposed acquisition of ITV's media and entertainment arm, a deal worth up to £1.6 billion.","Sky UK Limited agreed terms on July 6 to acquire ITV Media and Entertainment Holdings Ltd. Nandy said she was considering intervention on public-interest grounds: the free expression of opinion in news media, plurality of views in news media, and plurality of persons controlling media enterprises.","## New test proposed","The Culture Secretary also proposed a new public-interest consideration covering the variety of high-quality on-demand programmes — a change that would require legislation to amend section 58 of the Enterprise Act 2002.","Sky and ITV have until 09:00 on Oct. 20 to make representations. No final decision has been taken."],"sources":[{"name":"UK Government — Statement to Parliament by Culture Secretary Lisa Nandy (Oct 15, 2026)","url":"https://www.advanced-television.com/2026/10/15/culture-secretary-minded-to-intervene-in-sky-itv-deal/","role":"primary"},{"name":"The Times (Oct 15, 2026) — Nandy intervention report","url":"https://www.thetimes.com/business/companies-markets/article/lisa-nandy-intervene-itv-sky-775cnvzw0","role":"corroboration"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","notes":"Sky UK agreed terms July 6, 2026 for ITV Media and Entertainment Holdings Ltd (up to £1.6bn); Nandy 'minded to intervene' citing three plurality grounds plus a proposed new on-demand public-interest ground (requires Enterprise Act 2002 s.58 amendment); response deadline 09:00 Oct 20; no final decision taken. Corroborated by The Times (Oct 15)."}},{"id":"art-0129-japan-g20-fx-urgency-2026","slug":"japan-urges-g20-watch-fx-moves-high-sense-urgency","headline":"Japan Tells G20 to Watch Currency Moves “With a High Sense of Urgency”","socialHeadline":"Finance Minister Satsuki Katayama's warning in Bangkok came as the yen hovered near 159 to the dollar; G20 leaders issued no joint statement","summary":"Japanese Finance Minister Satsuki Katayama told G20 counterparts in Bangkok on Thursday that authorities must watch exchange-rate moves 'with a high sense of urgency,' as the yen's persistent weakness revives intervention speculation. G20 leaders issued no joint communique.","category":"Business","tags":["Japan","G20","yen","currencies","Satsuki Katayama"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-yen-fx-g20-20261015-0-daa1dc17-409c-4b1f-bc74-77fa93942425.webp","alt":"Illustration of yen and dollar symbols with a magnifying glass over a market chart on a navy background","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["Japanese Finance Minister Satsuki Katayama told G20 counterparts in Bangkok on Thursday that authorities must watch exchange-rate moves “with a high sense of urgency,” as the yen's persistent weakness revives speculation about intervention.","“We must closely watch financial market developments with a high sense of urgency,” Katayama said at the gathering, held on the sidelines of the annual IMF and World Bank meetings. She linked the concern to the yen's weakness raising import costs, including fuel, with the currency hovering near 159 to the dollar.","## No joint statement","G20 finance leaders re-confirmed their standing commitment on currency policy but produced no joint communique or chair's statement from the meeting."],"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — Japan tells G20 must watch FX moves with high sense of urgency","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/japan-tells-g20-must-watch-fx-moves-with-high-sense-urgency-2026-10-15/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Seoul Economic Daily — G20 Bangkok FX coverage","url":"https://en.sedaily.com/finance/2026/10/15/korea-japan-extend-10-billion-currency-swap-to-2029","role":"corroboration"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","notes":"Katayama on-record at G20 finance gathering, Bangkok, Oct 15, 2026; quote via Reuters; meeting on IMF/World Bank sidelines; no communique or chair's statement; yen near 159/USD; import-cost concern incl. fuel. Corroborated by Seoul Economic Daily."}},{"id":"art-0130-hasan-execution-livestream-poll-2026","slug":"most-americans-oppose-livestreaming-nidal-hasan-execution-poll","headline":"Eight in 10 Americans Oppose Livestreaming Hasan Execution, Poll Finds","socialHeadline":"The ABC News/Washington Post/Ipsos poll found opposition across party lines — even as the Pentagon insists December's firing-squad execution will be broadcast","summary":"Eight in 10 Americans say the execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan should not be livestreamed, according to a new ABC News/Washington Post/Ipsos poll — even as the Pentagon insists the December firing-squad execution will be broadcast.","category":"US","tags":["Nidal Hasan","Fort Hood","poll","death penalty","Pentagon"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","status":"PUBLISHED","breaking":false,"editorPick":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null,"image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-hasan-execution-poll-202610-0-86003338-c7ee-478a-b8f2-523a808e8638.webp","alt":"Illustration of a ballot box with poll-result bars and a scales-of-justice emblem on a navy background","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"body":["Eight in 10 Americans say the execution of former Army officer Nidal Hasan should not be livestreamed, according to a new ABC News/Washington Post/Ipsos poll released Thursday.","Hasan was convicted of killing 13 people and wounding 32 in the 2009 shooting at Fort Hood, Texas. His execution, scheduled for December by firing squad, would be the Army's first since 1961.","Opposition spans party lines: 91% of Democrats, 83% of independents and 64% of Republicans oppose livestreaming, the poll found. Even among those who support the firing-squad execution itself, 69% oppose broadcasting it.","## Pentagon insists it will be broadcast","Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth has vowed the execution would be livestreamed, and a Pentagon official said Tuesday: “The Secretary is correct. It will be live streamed.” ABC reported that President Trump and his advisers are weighing whether to drop the plan amid concerns about anti-American propaganda; Vice President JD Vance said he would not watch."],"sources":[{"name":"ABC News / Washington Post / Ipsos poll (Oct 15, 2026), via Political Wire","url":"https://politicalwire.com/2026/10/15/big-majority-oppose-livestreaming-execution/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Political Wire — poll coverage and reprints","url":"https://politicalwire.com/2026/10/15/big-majority-oppose-livestreaming-execution/","role":"corroboration"}],"verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T14:12:47Z","notes":"Ipsos KnowledgePanel poll released Oct 15, 2026: 8 in 10 oppose livestreaming; 91% D / 83% I / 64% R oppose; 69% of execution supporters still oppose livestream. Hasan convicted (2009 Fort Hood: 13 killed, 32 wounded); December execution by firing squad; Army's first since 1961. Hegseth vowed livestream; Pentagon official confirmed Tuesday; Trump/advisers mulling reversal per ABC; Vance won't watch. Distinct new development vs published pentagon-livestream-firing-squad-execution-fort-hood-2026 and jd-vance-firing-squad-execution-remarks (dedup clean). Figures from ABC's reporting, carried by Political Wire and reprints."}},{"id":"art-0131-jalen-hurts-ruled-out-panthers-2026-10-15","slug":"jalen-hurts-ruled-out-panthers-blood-clot-2026","headline":"Eagles Rule Out Jalen Hurts vs. Panthers After Blood Clot in Leg Shifts During the Week","socialHeadline":"Jalen Hurts is OUT Sunday vs. the Panthers — a blood clot in his leg moved this week, and the Eagles say his health comes first","summary":"The Philadelphia Eagles have ruled quarterback Jalen Hurts out of Sunday's Week 6 game against Carolina after a superficial blood clot in his leg shifted during the week. The team said a Wednesday-night ultrasound prompted the decision; backup Tanner McKee is expected to start.","body":["The Philadelphia Eagles ruled quarterback Jalen Hurts out of Sunday's Week 6 game against the Carolina Panthers after a superficial blood clot in his leg shifted during the week, the team announced Thursday.","In a statement, the Eagles said Hurts sought treatment for his calf on Oct. 8 after being cleated in the team's Oct. 4 game against the Rams. An ultrasound taken the following Saturday — after the team's flight to London — revealed the clot, but team physicians and London doctors cleared him to play against Jacksonville.","Hurts played through it in London, completing 21 of 40 passes for 220 yards and a touchdown in a 19-17 loss to the Jaguars. A follow-up ultrasound on Wednesday night, however, showed movement in the clot, and the team shut him down.","\"His health and safety are our highest priority,\" the Eagles said in the statement, adding that there was no timetable for his return beyond Sunday's game.","## McKee expected to start","Backup quarterback Tanner McKee is expected to start in Hurts' place, according to reports. The Eagles, now 2-3 on a three-game losing streak, face a 2-2 Panthers team on Sunday.","The timeline makes the decision one of caution: the clot was stable enough for doctors to clear Hurts for the Jacksonville game, but the change detected midweek changed the medical calculus, and the team chose not to take the risk.","Blood-clot issues have ended seasons for NFL players before, and teams have grown increasingly conservative with vascular injuries in recent years. The Eagles gave no indication of how long Hurts might be sidelined.","## What remains unknown","The team has not said when Hurts will be re-evaluated or what benchmarks he must clear to return. NewsVeria will update this story in place when the Eagles provide a timetable."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","Philadelphia Eagles","Jalen Hurts","Injury","Carolina Panthers"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-15T21:10:00Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-media-generation-nv-hurts-rule-0-6fe97cc2-89ee-466e-8074-230f1143f51d.webp","alt":"Illustration of a football helmet beside a medical clipboard with a leg icon, labelled Medical Update","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — full text of the Philadelphia Eagles' official statement, Oct 15, 2026","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/eagles-qb-jalen-hurts-blood-clot-ruled-out-vs-panthers--flm-2026-10-15/","role":"primary"},{"name":"USA Today Eagles Wire — independent corroboration of the timeline and ruling-out","url":"https://theeagleswire.usatoday.com/story/sports/nfl/eagles/2026/10/15/eagles-jalen-hurts-blood-clot-statement-medical-timeline-panthers/92266420007/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Eagles official statement (via Reuters, opened): superficial blood clot in leg, revealed by Saturday ultrasound after London flight; cleared to play vs Jacksonville (21/40, 220 yds, 1 TD, 19-17 loss); Wednesday-night ultrasound showed movement; ruled out vs Panthers (Oct 18); backup Tanner McKee expected to start; Eagles 2-3, Panthers 2-2. Eagles Wire independently corroborates. No timetable beyond Sunday.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T21:10:00Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":true,"pinned":false},{"id":"art-0132-don-mattingly-phillies-manager-2026-10-15","slug":"don-mattingly-named-phillies-manager-two-year-deal-2026","headline":"Phillies Remove Interim Tag, Sign Don Mattingly to Two-Year Deal as Manager","socialHeadline":"It's official: Don Mattingly is the Phillies' full-time manager on a two-year deal — 'last year really wasn't my team,' he says","summary":"The Philadelphia Phillies have signed Don Mattingly to a two-year contract as their full-time manager, removing the interim tag he carried since late April. Mattingly went 79-55 after replacing the fired Rob Thomson and led the club to a wild-card berth.","body":["The Philadelphia Phillies removed the interim tag and signed Don Mattingly to a two-year contract as their full-time manager, the club announced on Oct. 14.","Mattingly took over on April 28 after Rob Thomson was fired with the team sitting at 9-19. The Phillies went 79-55 the rest of the way under Mattingly, surging 21-4 in a 25-game August stretch to claim a wild-card berth before falling to the Atlanta Braves in the National League Wild Card Series.","President of baseball operations Dave Dombrowski said the club pursued former Red Sox manager Alex Cora before turning to Mattingly, who was offered the job Saturday after Cora rebuffed the Phillies' approach.","Speaking to reporters, Mattingly promised changes and was candid about the transition: \"Last year really wasn't my team — it was Thomps' team,\" he said, referring to his predecessor. \"Now we get to build it the way we want.\"","## Coaching staff overhaul","The managerial news came with a broader staff shakeup. The Phillies fired hitting coach Kevin Long and infield coach Bobby Dickerson, and hired former Mets manager Carlos Mendoza as infield and third-base coach.","The club also signed reliever Tim Mayza to a one-year, $2.75 million contract, getting an early start on bullpen construction for next season.","Mattingly, the former Yankees star and longtime manager of the Dodgers and Marlins, now gets his first full offseason to shape a Phillies roster that underachieved badly in the season's first month before its summer revival.","## What comes next","With the manager in place, attention turns to the roster: the Phillies must decide how aggressively to retool a team that won 88 games but exited the postseason in the opening round. Spring training opens in about four months."],"category":"Sports","tags":["MLB","Philadelphia Phillies","Don Mattingly","Manager"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-15T21:10:00Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-media-generation-nv-mattingly-0-276949a5-9423-4c06-896a-a78ef324961a.webp","alt":"Illustration of a baseball manager's lineup card, a whistle and a diamond diagram","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Delaware News Journal — report of the Phillies' official announcement, Oct 14, 2026","url":"https://www.delawareonline.com/story/sports/mlb/phillies/2026/10/14/phillies-likely-to-name-don-mattingly-full-time-manager-report-says/92245915007/","role":"primary"},{"name":"NBC Sports (AP reporting) — independent coverage with Mattingly/Dombrowski press-conference quotes","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/mlb/news/philadelphia-phillies-bring-back-don-mattingly-as-manager-coaching-staff-suffers-brunt-of-late-season-failure","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Phillies announcement Oct 14 (via Delaware News Journal, opened): interim tag removed, two-year deal; took over April 28 after Thomson fired at 9-19; 79-55 record, wild-card berth, lost to Braves in NL Wild Card Series; Cora rebuffed pursuit, Mattingly offered job Saturday; fired hitting coach Kevin Long and infield coach Bobby Dickerson; hired Carlos Mendoza; signed Tim Mayza 1yr/$2.75M. NBC Sports independently corroborates with press-conference quotes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T21:10:00Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false},{"id":"art-0133-halpin-homer-guardians-alcs-game3-2026-10-15","slug":"halpin-homer-guardians-alcs-game-3-rays-2-1-lead-2026","headline":"Rookie Halpin's Go-Ahead Homer Lifts Guardians Past Rays 3-2 for 2-1 ALCS Lead","socialHeadline":"Petey Halpin, a rookie, just flipped the ALCS — his 5th-inning homer gave Cleveland a 3-2 Game 3 win and a 2-1 series lead","summary":"Rookie Petey Halpin hit a go-ahead two-run homer in the fifth inning as the Cleveland Guardians beat the Tampa Bay Rays 3-2 in ALCS Game 3 on Thursday, taking a 2-1 series lead. Gavin Williams struck out nine over five innings for the win.","body":["Rookie Petey Halpin hit a go-ahead two-run homer in the fifth inning Thursday night, lifting the Cleveland Guardians to a 3-2 win over the Tampa Bay Rays in Game 3 of the American League Championship Series at Progressive Field.","The win gives Cleveland a 2-1 lead in the best-of-seven series, after the teams split the first two games — a 7-3 Guardians win in the opener and a 3-1 Rays victory in Game 2.","Halpin turned on an elevated 95.9 mph sinker from Griffin Jax and sent it 385 feet to right-center, erasing a 2-1 deficit. The blast was the defining swing of a night dominated by pitching.","Starter Gavin Williams was superb, striking out nine over five innings while allowing two runs, and José Ramírez chipped in two hits while Nathaniel Lowe added an RBI.","## Bullpen slams the door","Tampa Bay's only damage came in the fourth, on Chandler Simpson's two-run triple. From there, Cleveland's pitching took over: the Guardians retired 16 of Tampa Bay's final 17 batters.","The bullpen trio of Daniel Espino, Erik Sabrowski and Hunter Gaddis combined for four shutout innings, and closer Cade Smith recorded a four-out save to seal it.","Game 4 is scheduled for Friday in Cleveland, with rain in the forecast — a potential complication for both clubs' pitching plans.","## What comes next","The Guardians are two wins from the World Series. The Rays, who have dropped two of three in the series, will look to even things Friday before the series potentially returns to Tampa Bay."],"category":"Sports","tags":["MLB","ALCS","Cleveland Guardians","Tampa Bay Rays","Petey Halpin"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-15T21:10:00Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-media-generation-nv-alcs-game3-0-bed77804-c8ab-452f-b001-b22cf33316b0.webp","alt":"Illustration of a baseball arcing over an outfield wall with a scoreboard showing home 3, away 2","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Associated Press, via NBC Sports — Game 3 wire report, Oct 15, 2026","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/mlb/news/halpins-go-ahead-homer-flips-game-3-as-guardians-beat-rays-3-2-for-2-1-al-championship-series-lead","role":"primary"},{"name":"Sportsnet — independent game coverage confirming score, pitchers and key plays","url":"https://www.sportsnet.ca/mlb/article/gavin-williams-shoves-again-as-guardians-take-alcs-lead-over-rays/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"AP wire (via NBC Sports, opened): Guardians 3-2 Rays, ALCS Game 3, Oct 15, 2026, Cleveland, 2-1 series lead; Halpin go-ahead 2-run HR in 5th off Griffin Jax (95.9 mph sinker, 385 ft); Williams 9 K over 5 IP, 2 runs; Ramirez 2 hits; Lowe RBI; Cleveland retired 16 of last 17; Espino/Sabrowski/Gaddis 4 shutout IP; Cade Smith 4-out save; Simpson 2-run triple in 4th. Sportsnet independently corroborates. Game 4 Friday, rain forecast.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T21:10:00Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":true,"pinned":false},{"id":"art-0134-nba-gm-survey-spurs-wembanyama-2026-10-15","slug":"nba-gm-survey-spurs-wembanyama-title-favorites-2026-27","headline":"NBA GMs Pick Spurs, Wembanyama as Title Favorites in Annual Survey","socialHeadline":"The verdict is in: NBA GMs say the Spurs win it all and Wembanyama takes MVP — 77% of the vote","summary":"The NBA's annual general-manager survey is out, and the verdict is emphatic: the San Antonio Spurs are title favorites at 50%, and Victor Wembanyama is the runaway pick for MVP (77%), best defender (97%) and the player GMs would start a franchise with (93%).","body":["The NBA's annual general-manager survey, released Thursday by NBA.com and John Schuhmann, delivered a clear message about the 2026-27 season: the San Antonio Spurs are the team to beat, and Victor Wembanyama is the player around whom everything revolves.","The Spurs were picked to win the championship by 50% of GMs, comfortably ahead of the Oklahoma City Thunder at 43%. The Knicks and 76ers received one vote apiece.","Wembanyama's dominance of the ballot was striking. The Spurs star was projected as MVP (77%), the league's best defensive player (97%) and the player executives would choose first to start a franchise (93%). He also led voting for most adjustments to make, best international player, best interior defender and most versatile defender.","## Spurs' young core, Sixers' big summer","San Antonio's young core was voted the league's best at 87%, while the Philadelphia 76ers — who added LeBron James and Jaylen Brown this offseason — were voted the team with the best summer at 73%.","Elsewhere on the ballot: Cameron Boozer was projected as Rookie of the Year with 50% of the vote, Erik Spoelstra was voted the league's best coach at 43%, and Giannis Antetokounmpo's move to Miami was rated the most impactful acquisition at 53%.","The survey, conducted annually before the season, has a mixed record as a predictor — but it remains the clearest snapshot of how the league's decision-makers see the landscape. This year, that landscape has one unmistakable center of gravity in San Antonio.","## What comes next","The regular season tips off next week, when the Spurs' on-court product gets its first test against the expectations the league's own executives just set for it."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NBA","San Antonio Spurs","Victor Wembanyama","GM Survey"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-15T21:10:00Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-media-generation-nv-nba-gm-sur-0-42ba2065-d95f-4d62-be85-abffa91ca6b2.webp","alt":"Illustration of a basketball championship trophy beside a rising bar chart","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"NBC Sports — survey results confirming the NBA.com/John Schuhmann 2026-27 GM Survey release, Oct 15, 2026","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nba/news/nbas-annual-gm-survey-is-out-victor-wembanyama-spurs-get-a-lot-of-love-including-title-favorites","role":"primary"},{"name":"Sports Illustrated — independent coverage of the survey results","url":"https://www.si.com/nba/there-is-one-clear-winner-of-the-annual-nba-gm-survey","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"NBC Sports page opened: annual 2026-27 GM survey (NBA.com/John Schuhmann) released Oct 15, 2026; Spurs title pick 50% (Thunder 43%, Knicks/Sixers 1 each); Wembanyama MVP 77%, best defender 97%, start-a-franchise 93%, plus most-adjustments/best international/best interior/most versatile; Spurs best young core 87%; Sixers best offseason 73% (added LeBron James, Jaylen Brown); Boozer ROY 50%; Spoelstra best coach 43%; Giannis-to-Miami most impactful acquisition 53%. SI independently corroborates. Standalone NBA.com URL not returned by search — not guessed; underlying survey attributed in notes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T21:10:00Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false},{"id":"art-0135-oxfam-france-tax-inequality-2026-10-15","slug":"oxfam-france-sues-state-tax-inequality-2026","headline":"Oxfam France Takes the State to Court Over 'Tax Inequality'","socialHeadline":"Oxfam France is suing the French state, demanding a 2% tax on the wealthiest — 'breach of equality before tax'","summary":"Oxfam France has launched legal action against the French state for what it calls a breach of equality before tax, demanding compensation and measures including a proposed 2% tax on the wealthiest households' assets. If the state does not respond satisfactorily within two months, the NGO will file with the Paris administrative court.","body":["Oxfam France announced on Monday that it is taking the French state to court over what it calls systemic tax inequality, launching a legal action for \"breach of equality before tax.\"","The NGO sent a formal preliminary request to the state demanding compensation and concrete measures to end the situation — including the proposed 2% Zucman tax on the assets of the wealthiest households. If it receives no satisfactory response within two months, Oxfam will file its case with the Paris administrative court.","Oxfam France director general Cécile Duflot, a former government minister under François Hollande from 2012 to 2014, framed the case as a matter of constitutional principle, invoking Article 13 of the 1789 Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen, which states that taxation must be shared equitably among citizens.","\"There is a problem with the tax system and the funding of public services,\" the organization said, arguing that the wealthiest effectively buy the privilege of not following the same rules as everyone else.","## A long legal road","The assisting law firm, Ancile Avocats, says the case could take at least two years to work through the courts — a timeline Oxfam accepts, pointing to precedent: its 2021 climate lawsuit